id": "2118487751607697688", "type": "quoted"}, {"id": "2118451319061332429", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@Yngkvn @dwarkesh_sp There is a reason it is rare...\nhttps://t.co/oS5a0mLH9z", "url": "https://x.com/popetart9000/status/2118500123286331474"}, {"author_id": "1262941429686550529", "conversation_id": "2118449808402681911", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:23:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118499440118170022"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 12, "id": "1209960539390201864", "start": 0, "username": "dwarkesh_sp"}, {"end": 24, "id": "1740921954486636544", "start": 13, "username": "edtechceo_"}]}, "id": "2118499440118170022", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 14, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118449808402681911", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dwarkesh_sp @edtechceo_", "url": "https://x.com/kzdagoof/status/2118499440118170022"}, {"author_id": "206720696", "conversation_id": "2118449808402681911", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:15:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118497384162595154"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 12, "id": "1209960539390201864", "start": 0, "username": "dwarkesh_sp"}]}, "id": "2118497384162595154", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118449808402681911", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dwarkesh_sp I tell teams I use multiple models for the same reason — benchmarks keep reshuffling who's best at what, and a social-deception game is a brutal way to see that live.", "url": "https://x.com/cheneypiano/status/2118497384162595154"}, {"author_id": "10667972", "conversation_id": "2118449808402681911", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:05:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118495001277775964"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 12, "id": "1209960539390201864", "start": 0, "username": "dwarkesh_sp"}, {"end": 27, "id": "384666406", "start": 13, "username": "dillon_mulroy"}, {"end": 66, "id": "1810202562269954048", "start": 56, "username": "olam_labs"}]}, "id": "2118495001277775964", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 168, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118449808402681911", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dwarkesh_sp @dillon_mulroy Have you seen the work that @olam_labs are doing? Some cool overlap here good rest case", "url": "https://x.com/RhysSullivan/status/2118495001277775964"}, {"author_id": "2694715626", "conversation_id": "2118449808402681911", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:02:18.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118494146809692254"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 12, "id": "1209960539390201864", "start": 0, "username": "dwarkesh_sp"}]}, "id": "2118494146809692254", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 56, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118449808402681911", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dwarkesh_sp Yes— we’re also seeing in our multi-agent work that openAI has better imperfect information reasoning skills! Across a vast range of synthetic domains that we’ve tested", "url": "https://x.com/vartanshad/status/2118494146809692254"}, {"author_id": "411869974", "conversation_id": "2118449808402681911", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:01:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118494004983853450"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 12, "id": "1209960539390201864", "start": 0, "username": "dwarkesh_sp"}], "urls": [{"description": "Sharing since there’s BotC + AI discussions on Twitter: https://x.com/dwarkesh_sp/status/2118449808402681911", "display_url": "medium.com/@_leojiang/ai-…", "end": 90, "expanded_url": "https://medium.com/@_leojiang/ai-implementing-blood-on-the-clocktower-b915bc0590f7", "images": [{"height": 880, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118494006233677824/5NluzR3a?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118494006233677824/5NluzR3a?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 67, "status": 200, "title": "AI Implementing Blood on the Clocktower", "unwound_url": "https://medium.com/@_leojiang/ai-implementing-blood-on-the-clocktower-b915bc0590f7", "url": "https://t.co/fwvFk4tcPO"}]}, "id": "2118494004983853450", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118484468457750579", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dwarkesh_sp Summary of my latest BotC experiment using Fable 5.1: https://t.co/fwvFk4tcPO", "url": "https://x.com/leojiang/status/2118494004983853450"}, {"author_id": "1728813295119794176", "conversation_id": "2118449808402681911", "created_at": "2026-11-05T23:36:54.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118487751607697688"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 12, "id": "1209960539390201864", "start": 0, "username": "dwarkesh_sp"}]}, "id": "2118487751607697688", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 97, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118449808402681911", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dwarkesh_sp We have precious little time. Please dwarkesh if you make evals, spend your efforts on targets for good things.\n\nThis is cool but not good. Quality evals are signposts for optimization. They will be hillclimbed by some org eventually. Ask yourself, do you want this hillclimbed?", "url": "https://x.com/popetart9000/status/2118487751607697688"}, {"author_id": "1542195532038299648", "conversation_id": "2118449808402681911", "created_at": "2026-11-05T23:36:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118487597509206446"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 12, "id": "1209960539390201864", "start": 0, "username": "dwarkesh_sp"}]}, "id": "2118487597509206446", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 81, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118449808402681911", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dwarkesh_sp very cool!! love that more ppl r doing multi agent game evals", "url": "https://x.com/sensho/status/2118487597509206446"}, {"author_id": "411869974", "conversation_id": "2118449808402681911", "created_at": "2026-11-05T23:23:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118484468457750579"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 12, "id": "1209960539390201864", "start": 0, "username": "dwarkesh_sp"}]}, "id": "2118484468457750579", "note_tweet": {"text": "I'm probably one of the best BotC players in the world. I've tried many times over the past 2 years to get LLMs to understand the game, but it has consistently failed. The games involved intricate interactions between many characters, which LLMs fail to track, at most they they reason about interactions between pairs of characters. E.g. imagine a Poppygrower game where the demon voted to kill a minion, which a Cannibal ate and got poisoned info, but Oracle got 0 because they're next to No Dashii, while the drunk Village Idiot got good on the demon and the sober Village Idiot is Cerenovus mad. This is reasonable for a human player to track, but I haven't been able to get LLMs to come close.\nLet alone understanding theory of mind, they have no idea what a real player would be thinking.\nJust lying convincingly is the least interesting part of LLMs + BotC imo. I've participated in an AI Werewolf tournament and the best bot I've made just lied about the rules of the game and said stuff like \"earlier the storyteller announced I was good, you just forgot\" to never get executed, which I think is as good as current LLMs can get.\nImo it would be far more interesting to get agents to simulate each other player's beliefs. E.g. assuming players have perfect logic, how can evil players maximize the number of valid worlds where the real demon isn't believed to be a demon. I couldn't get a pure LLM to come close, it needed a script to track worlds."}, "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 77, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118449808402681911", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dwarkesh_sp I'm probably one of the best BotC players in the world. I've tried many times over the past 2 years to get LLMs to understand the game, but it has consistently failed. The games involved intricate interactions between many characters, which LLMs fail to track, at most they they", "url": "https://x.com/leojiang/status/2118484468457750579"}, {"author_id": "1988244586238799873", "conversation_id": "2118449808402681911", "created_at": "2026-11-05T23:21:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118483833716945164"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 12, "id": "1209960539390201864", "start": 0, "username": "dwarkesh_sp"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/uYD5IO6MQe", "end": 107, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/NateLorenzen/status/2118483583853867390/video/1", "media_key": "13_2118483489129639936", "start": 84, "url": "https://t.co/uYD5IO6MQe"}]}, "id": "2118483833716945164", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 19, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118449808402681911", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dwarkesh_sp Cool project. \n\nWe've been doing this same idea with Fantasy Football. https://t.co/uYD5IO6MQe", "url": "https://x.com/PlayATW/status/2118483833716945164"}, {"author_id": "1006737080419078144", "conversation_id": "2118449808402681911", "created_at": "2026-11-05T23:14:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118482081668051083"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 12, "id": "1209960539390201864", "start": 0, "username": "dwarkesh_sp"}, {"end": 23, "id": "982157088418770945", "start": 1